// EDUVERSE chunk: sat — generated by build-split.js from canonical bank files. Do not hand-edit.
window.EDUVERSE_BANK_SAT = [{"id":"SATM01","subtes":"Math","domain":"Algebra","soal":"If 4x - 9 = 2x + 7, what is the value of x?","opsi":["4","8","12","16","2"],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Memindahkan suku yang memuat x ke satu ruas dan bilangan ke ruas lain memberi 2x = 16, sehingga x = 8. Memasukkan 8 ke persamaan memberi nilai 23 di masing-masing ruas."},{"id":"SATM02","subtes":"Math","domain":"Algebra","soal":"If 2x + y = 17 and x - y = 4, what is the value of x + y?","opsi":["7","8","9","10","13"],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Menjumlahkan persamaan yang diketahui menghilangkan y dan memberi 3x = 21, sehingga x = 7. Dari persamaan x - y = 4 diperoleh y = 3. Jumlah x + y adalah 10."},{"id":"SATM03","subtes":"Math","domain":"Algebra","soal":"A line in the xy-plane passes through the points (0, 3) and (4, 11). What is the y-coordinate of the point on the line when x = 6?","opsi":["15","13","17","18","12"],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Kemiringan garis adalah (11 - 3) dibagi (4 - 0), yaitu 2. Persamaan garis adalah y = 2x + 3. Untuk x = 6, nilai y adalah 2 dikali 6 ditambah 3, yaitu 15."},{"id":"SATM04","subtes":"Math","domain":"Algebra","soal":"A van rental company charges $45 per day plus $0.25 for each mile driven. A customer rents a van for 1 day and pays $95 in total. How many miles did the customer drive?","opsi":["120","150","160","180","200"],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Biaya sewa satu hari adalah 45 dolar, sehingga sisa biaya untuk jarak tempuh adalah 95 dikurangi 45, yaitu 50 dolar. Membagi 50 dengan 0,25 memberi 200 mil."},{"id":"SATM05","subtes":"Math","domain":"Algebra","soal":"What is the greatest integer value of x that satisfies the inequality 5x - 3 < 2x + 12?","opsi":["3","6","4","5","7"],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Memindahkan suku yang memuat x ke satu ruas memberi 3x < 15, sehingga x < 5. Bilangan bulat terbesar yang kurang dari 5 adalah 4."},{"id":"SATM06","subtes":"Math","domain":"Algebra","soal":"Line p has the equation y = -3x + 8. Line q is parallel to line p and passes through the point (0, -2). What is the value of y on line q when x = 2?","opsi":["-8","-4","2","4","8"],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Garis sejajar mempunyai kemiringan sama, yaitu -3. Garis q melalui titik potong sumbu y di -2, sehingga persamaannya adalah y = -3x - 2. Untuk x = 2, nilai y adalah -6 dikurangi 2, yaitu -8."},{"id":"SATM07","subtes":"Math","domain":"Algebra","soal":"A print shop models the total cost, in dollars, of printing posters with the equation C = 20 + 8n, where n is the number of posters printed. What does the number 8 represent in this model?","opsi":["The total cost, in dollars, for 8 posters","The cost, in dollars, for each additional poster","The initial fee, in dollars, before any posters are printed","The total number of posters printed","The discount, in dollars, applied to each poster"],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Dalam model itu, 20 adalah biaya awal yang tetap, sedangkan 8 dikalikan dengan jumlah poster, sehingga 8 menyatakan tambahan biaya untuk setiap poster tambahan. Biaya awal dinyatakan oleh 20, bukan oleh 8."},{"id":"SATM08","subtes":"Math","domain":"Advanced Math","soal":"What is the positive solution to the equation x^2 - 5x - 14 = 0?","opsi":["-7","-2","2","5","7"],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Persamaan dapat difaktorkan menjadi (x - 7)(x + 2) = 0, sehingga penyelesaiannya adalah 7 dan -2. Penyelesaian yang bernilai positif adalah 7."},{"id":"SATM09","subtes":"Math","domain":"Advanced Math","soal":"The function f is defined by f(x) = x^2 - 6x + 5. What is the minimum value of f?","opsi":["-9","-5","-4","3","5"],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Melengkapkan kuadrat memberi f(x) = (x - 3)^2 - 4. Bentuk kuadrat tidak pernah negatif, sehingga nilai terkecil tercapai saat x = 3 dan nilainya adalah -4."},{"id":"SATM10","subtes":"Math","domain":"Advanced Math","soal":"A bacteria culture starts with 120 bacteria and doubles every 3 hours. Assuming no bacteria die, how many bacteria are present after 12 hours?","opsi":["480","960","1440","1920","3840"],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Selama 12 jam terjadi 4 kali penggandaan, karena 12 dibagi 3 adalah 4. Jumlah bakteri menjadi 120 dikali 2 pangkat 4, yaitu 120 dikali 16, yaitu 1920."},{"id":"SATM11","subtes":"Math","domain":"Advanced Math","soal":"If (2x + 3)(x - 4) is written in the form ax^2 + bx + c, where a, b, and c are constants, what is the value of b?","opsi":["-5","-8","5","8","-12"],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Menjabarkan perkalian memberi 2x^2 - 8x + 3x - 12, yaitu 2x^2 - 5x - 12. Koefisien dari x adalah -5."},{"id":"SATM12","subtes":"Math","domain":"Advanced Math","soal":"The mass, in grams, of a substance after x hours is modeled by the function f(x) = 500(0.8)^x. What is the mass, in grams, of the substance after 2 hours?","opsi":["256","320","360","420","500"],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Untuk x = 2, nilai fungsi adalah 500 dikali 0,8 pangkat 2, yaitu 500 dikali 0,64, yaitu 320 gram."},{"id":"SATM13","subtes":"Math","domain":"Advanced Math","soal":"If √(2x + 1) = 5, what is the value of x?","opsi":["7","9","10","11","12"],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Menguadratkan masing-masing ruas memberi 2x + 1 = 25, sehingga 2x = 24 dan x = 12. Pemeriksaan: akar kuadrat dari 25 adalah 5."},{"id":"SATM14","subtes":"Math","domain":"Advanced Math","soal":"The graphs of y = x^2 and y = 2x + 3 intersect at two points in the xy-plane. What is the sum of the x-coordinates of these points?","opsi":["-2","-1","2","3","4"],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Titik potong memenuhi x^2 = 2x + 3, yaitu x^2 - 2x - 3 = 0. Pemfaktoran memberi (x - 3)(x + 1) = 0, sehingga koordinat x adalah 3 dan -1. Jumlahnya adalah 2."},{"id":"SATM15","subtes":"Math","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","soal":"A jacket costs $120 before discounts. The store applies a 30% discount, and then a 10% tax is added to the discounted price. What is the final amount paid, in dollars?","opsi":["$84.00","$88.00","$90.00","$92.40","$96.00"],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Setelah diskon 30%, harga menjadi 70% dari 120 dolar, yaitu 84 dolar. Pajak 10% dari 84 dolar adalah 8,40 dolar, sehingga jumlah akhir adalah 84 ditambah 8,40, yaitu 92,40 dolar."},{"id":"SATM16","subtes":"Math","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","soal":"For the data set 6, 8, 11, 14, 21, what is the difference between the mean and the median?","opsi":["1","0","2","3","5"],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Jumlah data adalah 60, sehingga rata-rata adalah 60 dibagi 5, yaitu 12. Nilai tengah dari data yang sudah terurut adalah 11. Selisih rata-rata dan nilai tengah adalah 12 dikurangi 11, yaitu 1."},{"id":"SATM17","subtes":"Math","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","soal":"A bag contains 5 red marbles, 3 blue marbles, and 2 green marbles, all identical except for color. Two marbles are drawn at random, one after the other, without replacement. What is the probability that both marbles drawn are red?","opsi":["1/4","1/5","2/9","1/3","1/2"],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Peluang terambil merah pada pengambilan awal adalah 5 dari 10. Setelah satu merah terambil tanpa pengembalian, tersisa 4 merah dari 9 kelereng. Mengalikan peluang itu memberi 20 per 90, yaitu 2 per 9."},{"id":"SATM18","subtes":"Math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","soal":"A right triangle has legs of length 9 units and 12 units. What is the area of the triangle, in square units?","opsi":["27","36","45","48","54"],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Luas segitiga siku-siku adalah setengah dikali hasil kali panjang sisi siku-sikunya, yaitu setengah dikali 9 dikali 12, yaitu 54 satuan luas."},{"id":"SATM19","subtes":"Math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","soal":"A circle has a radius of 6 units. What is the area of the circle, in square units?","opsi":["12π","36π","24π","48π","6π"],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Luas lingkaran adalah π dikali kuadrat jari-jari, yaitu π dikali 36, yaitu 36π satuan luas."},{"id":"SATM20","subtes":"Math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","soal":"In a right triangle, one acute angle is A. The side opposite angle A has length 3 units, and the hypotenuse has length 5 units. What is the value of sin(A)?","opsi":["3/4","4/5","5/3","3/5","5/4"],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Sinus suatu sudut lancip dalam segitiga siku-siku adalah perbandingan panjang sisi di depan sudut itu dengan panjang sisi miring, yaitu 3 dibagi 5."},{"id":"SATRW01","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Craft and Structure","soal":"The town archive keeps letters written by dockworkers in the 1890s. At first glance the letters seem ordinary, recording wages, weather, and family news. Yet read together, they form a ______ account of daily life, one that official port records, focused only on cargo and tolls, never capture.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","opsi":["fanciful","fragmented","detailed","cautious","reluctant"],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Surat-surat itu bila dibaca bersama memberi gambaran kehidupan sehari-hari yang tidak ada dalam catatan pelabuhan yang hanya mencatat muatan dan pungutan. Kata yang tepat menggambarkan gambaran yang rinci dan menyeluruh. Kata lain tidak cocok: surat-surat itu tidak khayalan, tidak terpecah-pecah maknanya, tidak berhati-hati, dan tidak enggan."},{"id":"SATRW02","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Craft and Structure","soal":"For years, visitors to the Marlow marsh assumed the tall reeds were a sign of a healthy wetland. Biologist Ana Reyes thought otherwise. She measured water flow at twenty sites and found that the densest reed beds grew where old drainage channels had blocked natural tides. In the open tidal flats, shorter native grasses thrived. Reyes argues that the reeds are not proof of health but a symptom of blocked water.\n\nWhich choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","opsi":["It presents a common assumption, then offers research that challenges it and proposes a different interpretation.","It traces the history of the marsh from its formation to the present day.","It compares the growth rates of reeds and native grasses in controlled experiments.","It explains how drainage channels were built and why they were later abandoned.","It argues that all tall reeds should be removed from wetlands immediately."],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Teks membuka dengan anggapan pengunjung, lalu menyajikan pengukuran Reyes yang menentang anggapan itu, dan menutup dengan tafsiran lain tentang alang-alang. Teks tidak menelusuri sejarah rawa, tidak membandingkan laju tumbuh dalam percobaan terkendali, tidak menjelaskan pembangunan saluran, dan tidak menuntut pencabutan semua alang-alang."},{"id":"SATRW03","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Craft and Structure","soal":"Text 1: Novelist Priya Desai says she writes her first drafts by hand because the slower pace forces her to choose each sentence with care. She claims the practice makes her later revisions shorter and more focused.\n\nText 2: Writing teacher Tomas Vega agrees that slow drafting can help some writers, but he warns that it can also become a habit that delays finishing a book. For writers who already revise heavily, he suggests, speed matters more than deliberation.\n\nBased on the texts, how would Vega respond to Desai's claim?","opsi":["By denying that handwriting has any effect on revision.","By arguing that all writers should draft quickly to finish books.","By claiming that Desai's revisions are longer than she admits.","By suggesting that handwriting is useful only for experienced novelists.","By accepting a possible benefit of slow drafting while noting a drawback for some writers."],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Vega setuju draf lambat dapat membantu sebagian penulis, tetapi memperingatkan kebiasaan itu dapat menunda penyelesaian buku dan menyarankan kecepatan bagi penulis yang sudah banyak merevisi. Tanggapan yang tepat merangkum penerimaan manfaat sekaligus catatan kelemahan itu."},{"id":"SATRW04","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Craft and Structure","soal":"The lighthouse keeper's logbooks are ______ documents: brief entries about storms, ships, and repairs, written without flourish. Yet their very plainness makes them valuable to historians, who can trace decades of coastal weather in a few hundred pages.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","opsi":["ornate","spare","speculative","hostile","hurried"],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Entri-entri itu singkat dan tanpa hiasan bahasa, dan kesederhanaan itulah yang membuatnya berharga. Kata yang tepat menggambarkan gaya yang ringkas dan tanpa hiasan. Kata yang berarti penuh hiasan bertentangan dengan isi teks, sedangkan kata yang berarti dugaan, permusuhan, atau tergesa-gesa tidak didukung teks."},{"id":"SATRW05","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Craft and Structure","soal":"When the city of Halden replaced its downtown parking lot with a small orchard, critics predicted the trees would be vandalized within months. Five years later, the orchard still stands, tended by volunteers who harvest fruit for a food pantry. The city credits a simple rule: anyone may pick fruit, but no one may pick more than a small bag. Halden's experience is often cited by planners who argue that shared spaces survive when use is open but bounded.\n\nWhich choice best states the function of the discussion of Halden in the text?","opsi":["To prove that all parking lots should become orchards.","To explain how volunteers learned to care for fruit trees.","To criticize cities that build parking lots downtown.","To illustrate how a shared space can succeed under a clear limit on use.","To describe the history of food pantries in Halden."],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Contoh Halden menunjukkan ruang bersama yang bertahan karena aturan sederhana tentang batas pengambilan buah, dan contoh itu dipakai perencana sebagai ilustrasi prinsip ruang bersama yang terbuka tetapi berbatas. Teks tidak membuktikan semua lahan parkir harus menjadi kebun, tidak menjelaskan cara relawan belajar, tidak mengkritik kota, dan tidak menguraikan sejarah dapur pangan."},{"id":"SATRW06","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Craft and Structure","soal":"Glassblower Ines Mora works with molten glass that cools within minutes. She must shape each piece quickly, yet her movements look unhurried. Observers often describe her work as ______: every gesture appears planned, even when she adjusts to a sudden change in the glass.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","opsi":["hesitant","deliberate","reckless","secretive","playful"],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Gerakan Mora tampak tenang dan setiap gerakannya tampak direncanakan, bahkan saat ia menyesuaikan diri dengan perubahan mendadak. Kata yang tepat menggambarkan gerakan yang disengaja dan terencana. Kata yang berarti ragu, sembrono, tertutup, atau main-main tidak sesuai dengan gambaran gerakan yang terencana itu."},{"id":"SATRW07","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Craft and Structure","soal":"A study of 200 office workers found that those who took a short walk at midday reported better focus in the afternoon than those who stayed at their desks. The researchers caution, however, that the study lasted only two weeks and relied on self-reported focus. They suggest longer studies with direct measures of attention before employers draw firm conclusions.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?","opsi":["Midday walks guarantee better focus for all office workers.","Employers should require all workers to walk at midday.","Self-reported focus is a reliable measure of attention.","Two-week studies settle the question of lasting benefits.","A study found a link between midday walks and afternoon focus, but its limits mean the finding should be treated as preliminary."],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Penelitian menemukan kaitan antara jalan siang dan fokus sore, tetapi peneliti sendiri mengingatkan durasi pendek dan ukuran laporan diri, lalu menyarankan penelitian lebih panjang. Gagasan utama merangkum temuan sekaligus batas itu, tanpa mengubahnya menjadi jaminan atau anjuran wajib."},{"id":"SATRW08","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Information and Ideas","soal":"In the highlands of northern Luzon, farmers keep small plots of traditional rice varieties alongside modern high-yield rice. The traditional varieties produce less grain, but they survive floods and poor soil that damage modern plants. Agronomist Lila Tan found that families growing both types lost fewer harvests in bad years than families growing only modern rice. Tan concludes that keeping older varieties is not nostalgia; it is a practical safeguard against unpredictable weather.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?","opsi":["Growing traditional rice alongside modern rice helps farming families withstand bad weather, despite lower yields.","Modern rice always produces more grain than traditional varieties in every condition.","Farmers in northern Luzon refuse to grow modern rice.","Traditional rice varieties are grown only for cultural celebrations.","Floods and poor soil no longer affect rice farming in the highlands."],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Keluarga yang menanam kedua jenis padi kehilangan lebih sedikit panen pada tahun buruk karena varietas lama bertahan menghadapi banjir dan tanah miskin, meski hasilnya lebih rendah. Gagasan utama merangkum manfaat perlindungan itu beserta konsekuensi hasil yang lebih rendah."},{"id":"SATRW09","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Information and Ideas","soal":"The Harbor Museum displays a fishing boat built in 1912. The boat's hull was repaired many times, with patches of different wood added over decades. Curator Jon Park notes that the patches show which materials were available and affordable in each period. The museum therefore presents the boat not as a pristine original but as a record of changing local trade.\n\nAccording to the text, what do the patches on the hull show?","opsi":["The boat was rarely used after 1912.","The original builders used only one type of wood.","The museum restored the boat to its original condition.","The materials that were available and affordable when each repair was made.","Fishing boats in 1912 were built without any plan for future repairs."],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Kurator menyatakan tambalan menunjukkan bahan yang tersedia dan terjangkau pada tiap periode perbaikan. Teks tidak menyatakan perahu jarang dipakai, tidak membahas kayu asli pembangun, dan menegaskan museum tidak menyajikan perahu sebagai barang asli yang utuh."},{"id":"SATRW10","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Information and Ideas","soal":"A survey asked residents in three towns how often they visited the public library in a typical month. Researchers claim that towns with longer evening library hours tend to have more frequent visitors.\n\nTown | Evening hours per week | Residents visiting at least twice a month (%)\nAlderton | 4 | 18\nBriarfield | 10 | 31\nCedar Falls | 16 | 44\n\nWhich choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the researchers' claim?","opsi":["Alderton had 4 evening hours per week and 18% frequent visitors, a higher share than Briarfield.","Briarfield had fewer evening hours than Cedar Falls but a higher share of frequent visitors.","Cedar Falls, with 16 evening hours per week, had 44% frequent visitors, the highest share among the three towns.","All three towns had the same share of frequent visitors despite different evening hours.","Cedar Falls had the fewest evening hours per week but the highest share of frequent visitors."],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Tabel menunjukkan jam malam dan persentase pengunjung sering naik bersama: Alderton 4 jam dan 18%, Briarfield 10 jam dan 31%, Cedar Falls 16 jam dan 44%. Data Cedar Falls paling kuat mendukung klaim karena jam terpanjang sejalan dengan persentase tertinggi."},{"id":"SATRW11","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Information and Ideas","soal":"Orchards near wildflower strips produced more fruit than orchards surrounded only by grass, researchers found. The strips attracted wild bees, which visited blossoms more often than honeybees from managed hives did. When the strips were mowed early in the season, fruit production fell to the level of orchards without strips.\n\nWhich choice best states what can be inferred from the text?","opsi":["Honeybees visited blossoms more often than wild bees did.","Mowing wildflower strips early increased fruit production.","Orchards surrounded by grass produced the most fruit.","Wildflower strips had no effect on bee visits.","Wild bees attracted by wildflower strips contributed to higher fruit production."],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Kebun dekat strip bunga liar menghasilkan lebih banyak buah, lebah liar mengunjungi bunga lebih sering, dan produksi turun saat strip dipangkas lebih awal. Rangkaian itu mendukung simpulan bahwa lebah liar yang tertarik strip bunga liar berperan dalam produksi buah yang lebih tinggi."},{"id":"SATRW12","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Information and Ideas","soal":"Historian Ruth Adler argues that the growing use of railway timetables in the 1840s changed how ordinary people thought about time, making punctuality a public expectation rather than a private habit.\n\nWhich quotation from a town newspaper of the period best illustrates Adler's claim?","opsi":["'The new station is built of fine stone and stands at the edge of town.'","'Residents are reminded that the 8:15 train will not wait for latecomers, and clocks in the square have been set to railway time.'","'Ticket prices for the morning train remain unchanged this month.'","'The railway company thanks passengers for their patience during repairs.'","'Several farmers brought produce to market by cart this week.'"],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Kutipan yang tepat menunjukkan ketepatan waktu menjadi harapan umum: kereta tidak menunggu yang terlambat dan jam kota disetel mengikuti waktu kereta. Kutipan lain membahas bangunan, harga tiket, ucapan terima kasih, atau angkutan petani, tanpa menyinggung ketepatan waktu sebagai harapan umum."},{"id":"SATRW13","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Information and Ideas","soal":"Engineers in the coastal town of Nessa tested a small tidal turbine anchored beneath a pier. Unlike wind turbines, the device produced power on a predictable schedule, rising and falling with the tides. Over six months, it supplied steady electricity to the pier's lights and a nearby fish market, with no fuel and little noise. The engineers note, however, that the turbine's output was modest and that larger installations would need careful study of effects on fish and sediment.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?","opsi":["A small tidal turbine provided predictable, low-impact power on a modest scale, though larger use would require further study.","Tidal turbines produce more power than wind turbines in all locations.","The Nessa turbine supplied electricity to the entire town.","Fish and sediment were harmed by the Nessa turbine.","Tidal power requires fuel and produces significant noise."],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Turbin menghasilkan listrik sesuai jadwal pasang surut untuk lampu dermaga dan pasar ikan, tanpa bahan bakar dan hampir tanpa suara, tetapi keluarannya kecil dan instalasi besar memerlukan kajian dampak. Gagasan utama merangkum manfaat sekaligus batas itu."},{"id":"SATRW14","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Standard English Conventions","soal":"Before the hike, guide Tomas Reyes checks each hiker's survival kit. The kit must contain three ___ a compass, a whistle, and a waterproof map. Reyes also reminds hikers to carry water and to tell someone their planned route.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","opsi":["items,","items;","items:","items.","items"],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Daftar isi tas diperkenalkan setelah klausa lengkap tentang tiga benda yang wajib ada, sehingga tanda yang tepat adalah titik dua sebelum daftar. Koma atau titik koma tidak tepat untuk memperkenalkan daftar itu, titik membuat daftar menjadi penggalan kalimat, dan tanpa tanda baca kalimat menjadi tidak jelas."},{"id":"SATRW15","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Standard English Conventions","soal":"The town archive preserves documents donated by local families over the past century. The collection of letters, diaries, and photographs from the 1920s currently ___ in a climate-controlled room at the archive, where researchers can request to view the materials.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","opsi":["are housed","were housed","have housed","is housed","are being housed"],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Subjek kalimat adalah kumpulan dokumen yang berbentuk tunggal, dan keterangan waktu menunjukkan keadaan saat ini, sehingga kata kerja yang tepat berbentuk tunggal masa kini dan bermakna disimpan. Bentuk jamak tidak sesuai dengan subjek tunggal, bentuk lampau tidak sesuai dengan keterangan waktu saat ini, dan bentuk yang bermakna menyimpan mengubah makna kalimat."},{"id":"SATRW16","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Standard English Conventions","soal":"My grandmother's photographs documented life in our fishing village for forty years. After the exhibition, the curator thanked my colleague and ___ for lending our family photographs to the museum. Visitors said the images helped them understand how the village had changed.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","opsi":["me","I","myself","mine","we"],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Kata ganti itu menjadi objek dari kata kerja berterima kasih, sehingga bentuk objek yang tepat dipakai. Bentuk subjek, bentuk refleksif, bentuk kepemilikan, dan bentuk jamak tidak tepat sebagai objek kalimat itu."},{"id":"SATRW17","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Standard English Conventions","soal":"On Tuesday, a science class from Riverton High School took a field trip. The trip was part of a unit on astronomy. The students visited the observatory, they learned how telescopes track distant stars.\n\nWhich choice best revises the sentence so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","opsi":["The students visited the observatory, they learned how telescopes track distant stars.","The students visited the observatory they learned how telescopes track distant stars.","The students visited the observatory, however they learned how telescopes track distant stars.","The students visited the observatory, they learned, how telescopes track distant stars.","The students visited the observatory, and they learned how telescopes track distant stars."],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Kalimat asal menggabungkan dua klausa lengkap hanya dengan koma. Perbaikan yang tepat menggabungkan kedua klausa dengan koma dan kata sambung. Kalimat tanpa tanda baca, kalimat dengan kata penghubung yang bukan kata sambung, dan kalimat dengan koma tambahan tetap tidak memperbaiki penggabungan itu."},{"id":"SATRW18","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Standard English Conventions","soal":"The trail to Mount Sora takes four hours to climb. The climb begins before dawn. Hiking to the summit, the view of the valley appeared suddenly through the clouds.\n\nWhich choice best revises the sentence so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","opsi":["Hiking to the summit, the view of the valley appeared suddenly through the clouds.","Hiking to the summit, the climbers saw the view of the valley appear suddenly through the clouds.","Hiking to the summit, the view of the valley was seen suddenly through the clouds.","While hiking to the summit, the clouds parted to reveal the view of the valley.","The view of the valley, hiking to the summit, appeared suddenly through the clouds."],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Frasa pembuka menggambarkan orang yang mendaki, sehingga subjek kalimat haruslah para pendaki. Kalimat yang tepat menempatkan para pendaki sebagai subjek yang melihat pemandangan. Kalimat lain menempatkan pemandangan atau awan sebagai pelaku pendakian, sehingga maknanya tidak masuk akal."},{"id":"SATRW19","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Standard English Conventions","soal":"Marco works as a librarian during the week. He also volunteers at a weekend book club. On weekends, Marco enjoys reading novels, playing chess, and to restore old bicycles.\n\nWhich choice best revises the sentence so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","opsi":["On weekends, Marco enjoys reading novels, playing chess, and to restore old bicycles.","On weekends, Marco enjoys reading novels, playing chess, and he restores old bicycles.","On weekends, Marco enjoys reading novels, playing chess, and restoring old bicycles.","On weekends, Marco enjoys to read novels, playing chess, and restoring old bicycles.","On weekends, Marco enjoys reading novels, to play chess, and restoring old bicycles."],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Semua kegiatan dalam daftar harus berbentuk sama karena semuanya menjadi objek dari kata kerja yang sama. Bentuk yang tepat memakai bentuk kata kerja berakhiran -ing untuk semua kegiatan. Campuran bentuk infinitif atau klausa membuat daftar tidak sejajar."},{"id":"SATRW20","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Standard English Conventions","soal":"The mill was built in 1875 and ground grain for nearby farms. The old mill still stands beside the river. ___ wooden wheel, though cracked, turns slowly when the water rises.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","opsi":["It's","Its'","It is","Its","Its's"],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Kalimat membutuhkan kata ganti kepemilikan sebelum kata benda roda kayu. Bentuk kepemilikan yang tepat tidak memakai apostrof. Bentuk singkatan yang berarti 'itu adalah' dan bentuk lain dengan apostrof yang salah tidak menyatakan kepemilikan."},{"id":"SATRW21","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Expression of Ideas","soal":"Many small towns have lost their local newspapers. Without a regular paper, there is no published record of council decisions. ___ residents often learn about town meetings only through word of mouth.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","opsi":["As a result,","In contrast,","Meanwhile,","Nevertheless,","Similarly,"],"kunci":0,"bahas":"Kalimat terakhir menyatakan akibat dari hilangnya surat kabar lokal dan tidak adanya catatan keputusan dewan, sehingga kata penghubung akibat yang tepat. Kata penghubung pertentangan, waktu bersamaan, penentangan, dan kesamaan tidak menyatakan hubungan akibat itu."},{"id":"SATRW22","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Expression of Ideas","soal":"The new bike lane was expected to reduce car traffic on Main Street, and planners had predicted a 15% drop in car trips. ___ car traffic remained steady during the first year, though bicycle use doubled.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","opsi":["Therefore,","For instance,","In addition,","As a result,","However,"],"kunci":4,"bahas":"Kalimat terakhir bertentangan dengan harapan penurunan lalu lintas mobil, sehingga kata penghubung pertentangan yang tepat. Kata penghubung simpulan, contoh, penambahan, dan akibat tidak menyatakan pertentangan itu."},{"id":"SATRW23","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Expression of Ideas","soal":"Notes:\n- A community garden in Elm Park opened in 2019 on a vacant lot.\n- Volunteers grow vegetables and donate about 200 kilograms of produce each year to a food pantry.\n- The garden also hosts free workshops on composting and seed saving.\n- In 2024, the city council voted to extend the garden's lease for ten years.\n\nA student wants to emphasize both the garden's charitable contribution and its educational role. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","opsi":["The community garden in Elm Park opened in 2019 on a vacant lot and received a ten-year lease extension in 2024.","The Elm Park garden donates about 200 kilograms of vegetables each year to a food pantry and hosts free workshops on composting and seed saving.","Volunteers at the Elm Park garden grow vegetables on a vacant lot that opened in 2019.","In 2024, the city council extended the garden's lease for ten years.","The garden hosts workshops on composting, but it donates no produce to local charities."],"kunci":1,"bahas":"Catatan menunjukkan sumbangan sekitar 200 kilogram hasil panen setiap tahun kepada dapur pangan dan lokakarya gratis tentang pengomposan dan penyimpanan benih. Kalimat yang tepat memuat kedua hal itu sekaligus. Kalimat lain hanya memuat tahun pembukaan atau perpanjangan sewa, atau menyatakan hal yang bertentangan dengan catatan."},{"id":"SATRW24","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Expression of Ideas","soal":"The history museum redesigned its farming exhibit to be more interactive. The new exhibit includes objects visitors can touch. ___ one display lets visitors grind grain with a stone replica, just as farmers did centuries ago.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","opsi":["However,","Nevertheless,","For example,","In contrast,","Otherwise,"],"kunci":2,"bahas":"Kalimat terakhir memberi contoh benda yang dapat disentuh pengunjung, sehingga kata penghubung contoh yang tepat. Kata penghubung pertentangan, penentangan, dan syarat sebaliknya tidak menyatakan hubungan contoh itu."},{"id":"SATRW25","subtes":"Reading and Writing","domain":"Expression of Ideas","soal":"Notes:\n- Marine biologist Dr. Sara Kim studies seagrass meadows off the coast of Busan.\n- Seagrass meadows store carbon in the soil beneath them.\n- When meadows are damaged by anchors and dredging, stored carbon can be released.\n- Kim's team mapped the meadows and proposed protected zones where anchoring is limited.\n- Local fishers helped choose zones that protect meadows without closing prime fishing areas.\n\nA student wants to emphasize the collaboration with fishers and the carbon benefit of protecting the meadows. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","opsi":["Seagrass meadows grow off the coast and store carbon in the soil beneath them.","Anchors and dredging can damage seagrass meadows and release stored carbon.","Dr. Kim's team mapped seagrass meadows to study how fast the plants grow.","By working with local fishers to set protected zones, Kim's team aims to safeguard seagrass meadows that store carbon while keeping prime fishing areas open.","Local fishers opposed all protected zones because the zones would close fishing areas."],"kunci":3,"bahas":"Catatan menunjukkan tim bekerja bersama nelayan setempat memilih zona lindung yang menjaga padang lamun penyimpan karbon tanpa menutup area tangkap utama. Kalimat yang tepat memuat kerja sama itu dan manfaat karbonnya sekaligus. Kalimat lain hanya memuat satu rincian, menyatakan tujuan pemetaan yang tidak ada dalam catatan, atau bertentangan dengan catatan tentang peran nelayan."}];
